3. Add 1 to '2' -> [4, 3, 3, 3, 4]. Product = $4 \times 3 \times 3 \times 3 \times 4 = 432$.
4. Add 1 to '3' -> [4, 3, 2, 4, 4]. Product = 384.
5. Add 1 to '4' -> [4, 3, 2, 3, 5]. Product = 360.

